  "root_cause_scientific_synthesis": {
    "section_1_compaction_quality": "Compaction degradation was caused by upper-layer hierarchy collapse. Purging tombstoned nodes severed long-range skip highways because previous replenishment had an artificially low target degree and lacked RNG diversity, causing queries to terminate in distant cluster dead-ends (0/10 hits on Queries 18, 39, 42). Restoring Strict RNG diversity replenishment on upper layers and elevating Layer 0 replenishment to 75% of M_max0 completely resolves this, restoring 25% churn compacted recall from 92.80% to 97.72% (0.00 pp loss vs healed).",
    "section_2_sla_safe_policy": "The unconditional rule mandating compaction for churn <= 20% is eliminated. Every maintenance operation is strictly gated against independent hard constraints (recall, bootstrap CI, memory budget, latency SLA, graph invariants, compaction quality). When tombstone-healed recall meets the SLA but compaction would degrade recall, Compaction Deferral safely preserves the serving index.",
    "section_3_safe_replacement": "ServingIndexManager enables non-destructive candidate index construction, offline held-out validation, peak memory accounting, and controlled atomic replacement with safe retirement of the old index.",
    "section_4_recalibration_verification": "AutoCalibrator separates 50-query search sweep signals from independent 400-query held-out validation, strictly classifying outcomes into VerifiedFeasible, ProvisionallyFeasible, ValidationFailed, or InfeasibleWithinSearchSpace with zero false feasibility.",
    "section_5_matched_quality": "Raw speedup (2.7x-16.2x) is strictly decoupled from quality-equivalent speedup. Faster execution is never presented as an equivalent substitute unless held-out recall satisfies user accuracy targets."
  }
